19/08/99

   o ScriptSet - Added Read globally from next unread area to my
       personal scriptset.
   o Zeus.Library - Added support for modem CONNECT strings of
       the format:

             comp<->modem  protocol     tx       rx speed.
       CONNECT 57600/V34/LAPM/V42BIS/28800:TX/31200:RX

       If any Zeus line connector (ZMailer and Connector currently) sees
       a connect string with ":RX" in it, it will report the connection
       baud as the RX (Receiving) baud rate.  Further changes to Zeus
       might make it capable of understanding split rates, but not
       today.

20/08/99

   o ZMailer - Added further validation to ARexx port to ensure no
       strings passed for configuration are too long.

28/08/99

   o ZGate - Now adds REPLYADDR kludges.  ZGate still makes use of
       it's own internal reply database, but this offers better
       protection from failures to it.

30/08/99

   o ZMP - Added loop-mail checking for Netmails which are routed back to
       your system.  Sends notification to possible looping system (last
       in Via lines) and also informs source of message.  A looped mail
       is placed in the BAD message area and not exported again.
   o ZMP - Doubled the size of bounce mails to 32KB, in order to overcome
       problems with Internet mails which are 99% control lines.
   o Control - This now works on OS 2 again :-(
   o Control - New argument and ToolType - "NoDataTypes".  Disables
       use of Datatypes for loading backdrop.  No, I haven't finished
       datatypes use yet...

31/08/99

   o ZMailer - Added dial list window.
   o Voyeur - Worked out why the slider never reacted.  Nasty little
       bug. I've fixed it, but actually disabled the slider anyway
       since it's no use...
   o ZMP - Added configuration items to disable netmail loop checking
       and how it works.
            NOCHKMAILLOOP     -- disable checking
            NOCHKMAILLOOPAKAS -- if checking is enabled, then
                                 we don't check all AKA's, only the
                                 address specified after the NODE
                                 config item.

01/09/99

   o Zeus.library - added a function to change a dock icon's imagery
       without having to remove and re-add the icon itself.

       void ChangeGadImage( struct Gadget *g, UBYTE *name )

   o ZMailer - Added support for the above function.  Now when ZMailer
       changes its icon it does not change the icon's position.

04/09/99

   o ZNewsXfer - Stupid mistake turned \r\n line endings into \n\n
       instead of \n\0.  Fixed.

06/09/99

   o FileManager - Fixed the long-known-about bug which stopped it updating
       file comments if there wasn't already some sort of file comment
       there.

08/09/99

   o ANSI Watcher - Started implementing public screen support.  Got most of
       it done in about five minutes, I've just got to add Pen allocation
       (which will need some magic if ANSI is to work on OS 2 as well).

11/09/99

   o ZNewsXfer - Added better support for multiple news hosts.  The LastNNTP
       file, which stores the last date you downloaded messages, now also
       stores which server that date is for (eg. LastNNTP_news.server.co.uk).
       You will need to invoke ZNewsXfer with the LASTDATE argument to
       reinitialise this system for each server.
       *There is still a problem with this program - it works fine on some
       news servers, but on others (like at Freeserve) it corrupts the text.

14/09/99

   o ZGate - Fixed a bug where ZGate would hang on Packet->E-Mail.  It was
       incorrectly generating temporary file names and could eventually put
       itself in an infinite loop.

15/09/99

   o ALL - Found that there *does* exist a Y2K bug in Zeus - the SAS/C 6.50
       mktime() function fails after 29th February 2000 which made
       locating the problem difficult.  New code has now been written
       which should solve this last problem (which also caused the time
       in several places to be out by 6 or 1 hour due to another mktime()
       bug!).
   o zeus.library - Now contains a replacement for mktime() called
       MkTime() ...
   o FileControl - This now uses the new MkTime(), and all tests look good
       so far.

16/09/99

   o Control - Fixed condition where a windowed Control would not iconify.
       It was checking for other windows opened after itself (as it should
       on its own screen, but not on Workbench).

21/09/99

   o ZMP - Corrected serious problem which caused it to skip incorrectly
       terminated messages in packets (no LF on the last line).  I haven't
       seen any programs that create messages like this, but the 'hand
       made' FTSC Y2000 test packets are.

30/09/99

   o ZMP - Fixed a infinite loop in the loop mail handling system.

04/10/99

   o ZGate - Only one ZGate can run at a time.  I will implement code to wait
       for an existing ZGate to quit, but this will do for now.  The reason
       is the ZGate database - it's possible to get it out of sync or even
       for two ZGates to try to write to it at once.
   o ZGate - Improved handling of the index files.  It looks like it was
       limited to writing just 16KB of MSGID (etc.) data, no matter how high
       you set the index limit in Internet prefs.  It would certainly
       explain some odd behaviour I've seen with respect to some news
       messages being reply linked and others not.
       Hmm.. the 'odd behaviour' was really linked to a corrupt ZGate.idx
       file :-)  Which I'll blame on the old Idx routines :-)
   o ZGate - Wasn't setting the Private flags on netmails! Missed
       a swap from Big to Small endian on the attributes field.

12/10/99

   o ZGate - Handles Path: lines in newsgroups better.  Before, the path
       would be the from name in the message being gated even if you had a
       unique host name (i.e. User name is not filled in in Internet
       prefs), now it uses the actual host name itself.  This fixes
       problems with NNTP/UUCP type servers batching mail back to the BBS.

13/10/99

   o Zeus.Library - Added new function to allow the presence of default
       Internet names in the mapping configuration.

       BOOL FindMapInternetEntry( AREG(0) UBYTE *s, AREG(1) UBYTE *dom,
               AREG(2) struct FidoAddress *a, AREG(3) UBYTE *def_name )

       The default Internet name is indicated in the mapping config
       as "^", in the same way as "@" is used to indicated the user's
       real name.
   o ZGate - Added support for FindMapInternetEntry().  If a default
       Internet name is found, it's used, else the From name in the message
       is used (as it was before).
   o UpdateConfigs - Added option "MAP" to update mapping config.
   o Zeus.Library - The mapping system seems to have been a bit badly
       implemented:  Any item marked as default ("@", or with my new "^"
       Internet default marker) needed to appear before the item on which
       the message was remapped, for example:

               @Neil Williams,neil

       would remap a message for neil to Neil Williams.  But:

               neil,@Neil Williams

       would not.  This has been overhauled and fixed.

14/10/99

   o ZMailer - Yes, one L in dialing.

16/10/99

   o ZMF.Library - Fixed the quoter so it can handle Intershite-style
       inital-less quotes which start on the first column (worked in the
       E version - it was a C->E conversion problem).

23/10/99

   o ZGate - Spent much time working on the internal database. Hopefully
       it's all going to work brilliantly now.
   o ZGate - With luck, mailing lists will now address the To: field
       correctly, just like the magic for newsgroups.
   o MsgConfig - Correctly sets address domains if equal to 8 characters
       in length.
   o AreaChange.zeus - If there was exactly x pages + 1 item, you couldn't
       jump to that last item. Fixed.

24/10/99

   o All - Finally managed to get BOOPSI classes to compile here.  There's
       something wrong with the link libs I'm using, just temporarily
       pointing to SAS/C 6.2's link libs works fine.  Expect work on
       UserEditor and the List View class to be done now.
   o jplistview.gadget - Added support for Drawer Images (some code was
       already in there, I just added support for it and fixed the code).
   o jplistview.gadget - Now draws THIN left/right sides.  I intend to
       add code to check screen ratios, but for now it looks much better
       to me.
   o FileEditor - Added support for the jplistview drawer image for the
       "... parent" item.  It isn't perfect yet, it draws a little over the
       limits of the item height.

25/10/99

   o MsgControl - MsgAreasLoad() now searches for non-unique Unique fields.
       This causes a little bit of slow down on loading, but ensures the
       DataManager will always work.

26/10/99

   o UserEditor - Correctly "busy's out" the main window when subwindows
       open.
   o Manual - Added Chapter 13, DataManager.

27/10/99

   o AmiEx - Wrote an AmiExpress (/X) door emulation (XIM).  It's not 
       complete, but I intend to complete /X 3.0 emulation soon - as soon
       as I can find reliable /X 4 docs, I'll add in those extra commands
       too.  /X ARexx (AIM) to follow!
   o Zmf.Library - Re-enabled AddMarkedFile() - though I'm a bit cautious
       until I know why Nick commented it out.

28/10/99

   o ScriptSet - Wrote a groovy AddUpload.zeus script which allows the user
       to edit the File_Id.DIZ - also with countdown like this:
       "Edit Description? [Yes/NO] [5..4..3..]"

29/10/99

   o jplistview.gadget - If the string given for the list view to show was
       too long, jplistview would just draw over the right side boundary.
       Fixed - the string is drawn to width of the listview only.
   o jplistview.gadget - Hopefully reduced the amount of unnecessary
       redrawing done during slider-based scrolling.
   o ZMailer - ARexx port is now active while online. QUIT will not have
       any effect in this state, however. I recommend important scripts
       which use QUIT check if ZMailer has actually gone by looking
       for the port.
   o ZMailer - Added ARexx command ONLINE.  Return RESULT="Online" and
       RC=1 for online, RESULT="Offline" and RC=0 for offline.
       NB: reflects the state of the phone line, so even dialing out
       will return "Online".
   o ZGate - Added some code to detect a slightly corrupted database
       which hasn't been totally filled yet. If one is found the database
       pointer will point to the first record, but no data will be
       removed.

30/10/99

   o ANSI - The watcher defined ANSI code 21 to switch off intense/bold
       text. This didn't work with term, as term uses 22 - as I don't know
       which is correct, both 21 and 22 work in the ANSI watcher but you
       should use 22 in the Languages (for msg *bold*) settings etc.

31/10/99

   o ConvMsgToText - Added to it the features from my old DumpMsg program.
       These extra features are designed to allow ConvMsgToText to be used
       in automated ARexx processing easier:

   FILENAME  - File to output messages to (defaults to shell output)
   LINEWRAP  - Wrap lines to 80 columns
   PARSEHEAD - Output header in a form suitable for easy parsing via ARexx
   NOCTRLA   - Replace ^a (ASCII 1) with '^'

01/11/99

   o ZMP - Created an area import statistics base.  It needs to be better
       integrated, but works fine.  Stores Imported msg/tick number and
       byte total in Zeus:Config/Msg/MsgNetStats.dat.
   o ZMPStat - Prints the above data file in text form to the CLI.

04/11/99

   o ZMPStat - Completely rewrote to show stats in a similar way to how
       you use mbManager or similar.

10/11/99

   o ZGate - `From' address for mailing lists was sometimes incorrect
       (reflected that of the user not list) - Fixed.
   o Manual - Cleaned up some sections and made them easier to read.
   o Manual - Spent 4 hours working on the manual, writing new sections
       to chapters and setting up some appendixes with new and existing
       sections.  Also documented and cleaned up some ARexx functions
       (I had forgotten WriteMsg for some reason! :-)

13/11/99

   o Phoenix - Fixes to Archiver parts of the code and ARexx scriptset.
       No longer shows archivers you have set to No Show, and the Rexx
       doesn't stop on the first No Show.  The Arc Name CC of Phoenix
       returns "NO_SHOW" if the archiver can't be shown (it's the best
       workaround).

16/11/99

   o ZNM.Device - Fixed problem with Gotcha! mailer.  It requires
       totally accurate CMD_QUERY results which were not given with
       faked modem CONNECT responses (probably). Gotcha! now works
       fine, except that for some reason it redials ZMailer after a
       successful session... Whatever, ZNM calls don't cost anything.

18/11/99

   o Manual - Added chapter 14, Editing Your BBS.
   o ZMP - Changed the random-generator a bit. There was a good chance of
       the cut down datestamp used looping while old mail packets existed,
       as it looped every few months.
   o Voyeur - Nodes list window is now resizable.  And it looks like the
       jplistview gadget still overwrites the right edge sometimes.
   o Voyeur - Spent some time cleaning the code. It now produces no
       compilation warnings and implements GadTools correctly.
   o Voyeur - Implemented a menu structure. Main purpose is to provide
       window snapshotting features, although the ToolType/CLI window
       positioning will take precedence.
   o Voyeur - Snapshot now works.  See the new menus in >1.3 to snapshot
       the two Voyeur windows in any position. Note: while width is
       snapshotted on the nodes list window, height is currently not.

21/11/99

   o ZMP - Fixed crashes on messages longer than the buffer.  At the moment
       it just cuts the message off at that point. I'm working on
       implementing a system to extend the buffer when necessary, but it'll
       take a bit more work.. There's lots of inter-dependant modules :(

22/11/99

   o ZMF.Library - In 1.2 multipaths for file areas were broken.  It was
       saving the paths data out incorrectly so on reading it back, it
       appeared corrupt. Appologies about this. You'll either need to
       reconvert your old Paths data (Zeus made a backup on the 1.1 to 1.2
       conversion, so use the converter in the 1.2 upgrade pack) or redo
       the paths configuration.
   o ZMF.Library - Found a fixed a bug (long standing, i.e. NOT my fault ;)
       which caused the MultiPaths code to incorrectly report the free
       space on a drive - in effect, this caused the system to always
       think there was enough disk space available and so never use any
       other writable paths than the main one for saving files to.
   o ShowFilePaths - Added this new command to show the multi-paths of
       your file areas.  It does not show the main configured paths.
   o FileConfig - In multi-paths, the "R/W / Read" Cycle gadget did not
       work as the previous programmer (i.e. not me again! ;) was setting
       the value of the Cycle object by asking it to CheckMark itself...
   o Manual - Wrote some more on Multi-Paths in the Files chapter, adding
       undescribed features and highlighting what a flippin' fantastic
       thing it is (I've only just realised how good it is myself).
   o FileControl - Fixed ControlCode 1061 (Current File's path) to use
       MultiPaths.
   o FileControl - Modified ControlCode 1002 to support MultiPaths.
       If the argument is specified like "%1002:<AREA_NUMBER>|" then
       it will report the main configured path.  However,
       "%1002:<AREA_NUMBER> <FILE_NAME>|" will report the correct path
       for the given file name in that area.  Note that the two options
       are seperated by only a space.
       PLEASE NOTE: The Files/GetFile.zeus script used by some supplied
       example scriptsets uses this CC, in viewing and testing the file.
       This is why it has been MultiPaths aware, so a simple change can
       fix these scripts.

23/11/99

   o jplistview.gadget - I've been hard at work, and now this listview
       class has shifted-multiselect.  In plain language, that means
       that if you hold down shift and 'run' the pointer up and down the
       list with the left mouse button, the items will be selected.
       It isn't quite perfect yet, but it certainly make selecting lots
       of areas in File/Msg config much easier!
   o Manual - Wrote a description in the FidoNet chapter on ZMP's command
       line options and also a description on how to use ZMP's Tick
       facilities.
   o ZMP - Fixed many instances of file attach and Tick code to correctly
       use the file area's MultiPaths.  This has involved a lot of changes
       to the code, and I'd like everyone to be on the lookout for
       possible bugs - I am testing this myself, of course, but ZMP is
       quite important and there's a lot of it..
   o ZMF.Library - SaveFile() didn't check MultiPaths. Fixed.
   o FileControl - ARexx MoveFile was only partially MultiPath aware.
       Fixed.
   o ZGate - Just a side note, but I've discovered why often you see
       incorrect To: field in mailing list messages (when the message
       appears to be a new one, but is addressed To: someone).  The reason
       is that many people reply to someone's message in order to address
       their message to mailing list server.  The joys of Internet..
   o General - I'm confident all Zeus programs now correctly use
       MultiPaths.  The biggest problem is the most popular Zeus Freq
       utility, GoldFreq, doesn't.  Any other problems with it, please
       let me know.
   o Manual - More ABBERexx documentation.

24/11/99

   o Manual - Miscellaneous additions and changes (including removing a
       nasty (to me) remark which refers to phone code 44- and Britain as
       "England") and new sections on TextPreLoad and FileManager.
   o Developer Kit - Created a new developer kit, and while the includes
       are up to date (except for the E ones which I've not finished at
       all) the docs are frightningly out of date and incomplete.
   o ZMailer - Finally added the new random archive name generator from
       ZMP.  Packets are sent with the file name as the encoded
       destination address, bundles are sent with a time stamped/random
       name.
   o Manual - Wrote section in the FidoNet chapter on ZMPStat.

26/11/99

   o ZMailer - In Hydra it treated disk space as a signed value, so it
       couldn't handle more than 2GB of free space hence me not getting
       mail because :
       01BA006B.TU0 not enough diskspace: 193948 > -982214144
       ZMailer (and probably XPR) still cannot cope with >4GB - I'll
       work on it as soon as I get the OS 3.5 developer CD.

27/11/99

   o General - More fixes for partitions upto 4GB.  I'm waiting for the
       new v2.1 developer CD for more information on handling 64bit
       drive space values.

29/11/99

   o Control - It's now possible to load the backdrop image in via
       Datatypes. The Tooltype NODATATYPES now works. Until I get OS 3.5
       development info, you'll still need to set the palette correctly
       for your icons - Control locks the MagicWB colours so that any
       datatype background image doesn't mess with your colours.

01/12/99

   o FileManager - Cleaned up command line arguments to be more consistent
       with other programs, while also keeping compatibility.
   o FileConfig - MultiPaths will now ask you if you want to create
       directories if they don't exist.  It will not, however, blank out
       the path in the window if it can't be found or created - in case
       it's on an unmounted disk.
   o FileConfig - Added a `preview sort' - if you have a lot of areas,
       you can sort the list view by name, access, age limit or back to
       number to aid you in finding a specific area. The areas are always
       saved sorted by number. This will be more useful when implemented in
       MsgConfig, where you might have several thousand areas to search
       through.
   o FileConfig - Added keyboard control for the main list view - cursor up
       and down as usual, space to select an area, return (or E) to edit.

03/12/99

   o MsgConfig - Now has the same keyboard list control and sorting
       facilities as described for FileConfig.
   o MsgConfig - Since DataManager can't do it, MsgConfig now gives you
       the chance to Initalise message areas when you delete them,
       hopefully lowering the chances of old messages resurfacing when a
       new area is created with the same number as an old one.
   o ZNNTPXfer - Cleaned up code and log output. Also, I may have found
       the cause for failing with Freeserve's InterNetNews daemon - the
       INN daemon is broken!  NNTPGet also has problems with it, something
       to do with getting 2 connections when only one is needed.  Will
       research more after 6pm..

05/12/99

   o FileEditor - Full keyboard control of the listview, including
       shifted-up and down.  Space to select, return to enter an area or
       load a file's data.
   o Msg/FileConfig - Added shifted-cursor key scrolling to both.
   o Prefs/Internet - Removed the obsolete MIME code.

06/12/99

   o ZMP - Improved the duplicate file routine - when ZMP imports a
       duplicate file attach, instead of naming the first dupe as
       file.dup, the next as file.dup.dup, and so on, it will name the
       first as file.dup, then file.dup.1, then file.dup.2, etc.

08/12/99

   o MsgControl - Better handling of CR/LF in messages, and correctly
       ignores the `soft returns' put in by some extremely arcane PC
       programs (and PC users).
   o ZMF.Library - Quoter now strips out soft returns in messages.

09/12/99

   o ZMailer - I have spent literally all day working on ZMailer's
       Yoohoo/WaZoo implementation.  Needless to say it's now perfect.
       The main reason for it failing all the time was a missing Serial
       Clear - used to force a CRC out at a specific time.  Without it,
       the CRC was sent late and as such the remote system missed it.
   o ZMailer - Further refined time-out code: even in the event of a bad
       connection, ZMailer should hang up after no more than 2 minutes
       with no *real* data.  Previously, ZMailer could be kept online if
       the remote was continually sending bad data.

10/12/99

   o ZMailer - Further investigation into why QFront fails with ZMailer
       reveals that QFront might not see the first EMSI request, so now
       ZMailer will resend the request if it looks like a failing QFront
       connect. Trapdoor needs to send requests many times, too. If
       switching off Fast-EMSI allows QFront to connect, please re-enable
       it and test this please!

11/12/99

   o ZMailer - Tries to log Caller ID when in No Answer mode. In this
       case, if you want ZMailer to log CID when in No Answer but *not*
       in Online mode, you don't need to have Prefs->Ring Count set to
       2 or more.
   o ZMailer - Added a timeout to the RING detection. If you have ZMailer
       answering on 2 or more rings (e.g. for CallerID capture), ZMailer
       will time out the first ring after 1 minute.  What this means is
       if you get a call which hangs up after one ring, another call
       later (i.e. an hour, a day - but not within a minute) will have to
       ring twice, or whatever you have set, and will not take the earlier
       ring into account.  This should also help with the problem of
       ZMailer not logging all CallerID.

12/12/99

   o ANSI - I've taken a look through the code for the reason behind ANSI
       incorrectly scrolling under CGX (leaves artifacts behind) and why
       under AGA it can draw text over the bottom border of the screen.
       I've found a calculation for the number of lines on the screen
       which was wrong, fixing it fixed the AGA problem - I hope it also
       fixes the CGX problem too.

13/12/99

   o ZMP - Seems I broke AreaFix a little - it wasn't reporting when an
       area was linked in.
   o ZMailer - This didn't take any notice of the Check Carrier option in
       serial prefs!  I don't think Zeus, Connector or XprXfer do either;
       I'll check them later.  Essentially, all it does it fake the
       Carrier to be ON all the time - this means ZMailer will report
       "can't hang up" - but it will work, and switching off Carrier
       checks is normally only for local null-modem connections anyway.

15/12/99

   o FileEditor - Space selection of files didn't work well in unlisted
       files mode.

16/12/99

   o EMailGate - Added MIME encoding support (requires the external
       Base64Encode currently).  Also it now renames the archive to 8.3
       names - suitable for sending to PC e-mail tunnels.
   o EMailGate - Refinements, refinements, refinements.  Now checks the
       file name before doing any renaming - it must follow certain
       FidoNet bundle/packet naming rules.

17/12/99

   o ZMP - Added some more error checking.  Too long To/From/Subject
       fields in FTN messages will cause ZMP to abort the packet and
       report the error in ZMP.log.  Should cure some unexplained ZMP
       crashes.
   o Manual - There is now a whole chapter on EMailGate in the manual,
       written as an overview of FidoNet over Internet.
   o EMailGate - Now picks up the string to use for the MIME/Base64
       encoding program from an archiver named "MIMEenc".
   o Manual - Started on a Glossary to explain terms such as "Cron" for
       people who might not have seen them before.  Any suggestions for
       it?  Something you might have found confusing when first starting
       out?

18/12/99

   o ZGate - This could generate To/From/Subject lines that were one
       character too long or even more.  (As my new ZMP error checking
       has shown...)
   o MsgControl - Hopefully fixed a problem with window resizing. The
       border of the bottom most gadget now touches the window border on
       200 pixel high screens (e.g. NTSC), but this should not be a
       problem, apart from cosmetically.
   o ManyThings - Anything that uses the JPListView (e.g. File Editor)
       will now look for jplistview.gadget in Libs:Gadgets (usually
       Sys:Classes/Gadgets) as well as Libs: (and Zeus:Libs/ etc.)
   o ZSMTPSpool - Added this new program which produces Spool files out
       of E-Mails.  Use this in Internet prefs (check "ZSMTPSpool ?").
   o ZSMTPxfer - Sorry, but ZSMTPxfer is still work-in-progress - it
       works, but for some reason the SMTP terminator isn't being
       sent/received correctly. As 1.3 is going out before I finish it,
       watch our web site and ZeusNet for updates.
   o ZMF.library - Correctly removes kludges when quoting.

******************* Zeus 1.3 Fixed Feature Set **********************

20/12/99

   o ZMailer - Now has a Recent Log window, where the last 50 lines of
       the log file are shown, in the tradition of Gotcha and Trapdoor.

21/12/99

   o PostMan - Added a new argument: FORUSER=FOR/K. Specifying this on
       the command line changes the text under the icon on Control to
       reflect the name given here: eg: "SysOp: 1" and "CoSysOp: 3".
       The idea is to allow two or more PostMan's to run /and/ to be
       able to tell which PostMan shows who's message count.
   o ZMailer - Fixed enforcer hits in log window code, and updated event
       handlers so the window can be updated during a call.

23/12/99

   o ZGate - Fixed another situation where ZGate would assign the wrong To
       name for gated UseNet messages - it was taking the wrong Reference.
   o ZGate - Fixed problem where outbound newsgroup messages were spooled
       to the same file (so erasing the last message if spool files were
       merely copied to another directory).

24/12/99

   o Manual - Some minor work on the ARexx sections.
   o MsgControl - No longer incorrectly line wraps messages with ANSI
       codes.
   o ZSMTPxfer - Got it working! What you don't want to do, I've found,
       is send Nulls to a SMTP server. It doesn't like them.

28/12/99

   o DLG.library - Bumped version to 2. DLG Emacs now runs, but crashes
       on calling a DLG lib v2 function.
   o DLG.library - Exists() implemented.
   o DLGDoor - No longer forces ANSI Compression on.
   o DLG.library - Added stubs for all DLG library v2 functions. Code has
       been written for essential functions, but most do nothing - it is,
       however, good enough so far to run programs like EmacsDLG
       perfectly.

30/12/99

   o ZGate - Fixed another situation where ZGate could generate a To:
       field too long.

04/01/00

   o FileEditor - Fixed another description font preference bug. I had
       failed to update an internal structure if loading the prefs file
       failed, causing enforcer hits on loading the program afterwards.
       Yes, this is also the first real post-1/1/2000 fix and it's not
       a Y2K-date fix :)

05/01/00

   o ZMailer - Reworked some things in the hope that it no longer crashes
       on some configurations.
   o ZMailer - QFront systems should be able to call ZMailer now, if the
       crash&burn fix works.
   o ZMailer - Finally found the startup Enforcer hit - it was using the
       log window's list structure before it was initialised.
       MMU.library is god. I hope it makes it as part of OS 3.6.
   o Manual - New FAQ and Glossary items.
   o ZMF.library - Fix for quoter; it correctly detects old, already
       quoted to one level material with *your* initals, and so correctly
       treats it as old material (appending a ">") and not requotes it as
       if it were new.

07/01/00

   o ZMF.library - More work on sorting out Internet style initial-less
       quoting.  Hopefully it is now completely sorted.  Basically,
       the quoter treats any ">" quoted block by only putting an extra
       ">" onto it - it doesn't attempt to match it with any preceding
       lines, as it can't because there are no initals to match them to.
       With initialled blocks of quoted material, we can merge them
       together and do all sorts of clever things.
   o XPRxfer - Now checks the serial preferences and ignores carrier
       as per the Check Carrier option.
   o Zeus - The main BBS part also checks the Check Carrier option in
       serial prefs.  This was far more complex than with other programs,
       please try some tests of this on your configuration (basically,
       do you see any unusual carrier losses or any times when a user
       drops carrier and Zeus doesn't notice).
   o Voyeur - Asks for confirmation before booting users.
   o Zeus.Library - Displaying files (DisplayBltn, Display) should no
       longer exit when the user asks for Continuous output.

08/01/00

   o ZMP - Configuration reader now accepts a UseAKA item inside the
       linked addresses part of the AREA link (although it doesn't yet do
       anything; this is a major addition to ZMP and may take some time
       to finish).

       Take this fragment of ZMP.cfg as an example:

       NODE 2:442/107.0
       AKA  2:442/110.0

       AREA AMIGA_UK 0 .1 .2 .3 USEAKA 2:442/110 .4 .5

       Downlink .1, .2, .3 AND .5 receive Fido from 2:442/107.  Point 4,
       however, receives Fido mail from the Aka 2:442/110.
       Noteworthy points: any system linking in via AreaFix automatically
       receives mail from the NODE (main) address; netmails always come
       from the NODE address.
   o EMailGate - Sent non-mail files with their full local path,
       hopefully fixed - untested.
   o ZMP - WriteHdr() takes an optional linknode. If given, it will be
       used to get a UseAKA from address, and the given Destination
       address may be ignored.
   o ZMP - Same as above for WriteMsg().  Some inefficiency in that an
       element of the linknode is already passed - at some point this can
       be rewritten so that the element already passed is obtained from
       the linknode directly.
   o ZMP - Is now aware of the UseAKA option when writing Packet and
       Message headers.  Path/Seen-by is yet to do.
       [Tested okay: export to point .5 with AKA 107/110 was correct
       and hit free. Export to point .7 was still correct with main AKA
       101]

13/01/00

   o ZMF Docs - Wrote some more bits for the ZMF library documentation.
   o Control - Finally, at long last, got fully working datatype support
       for loading the background image.  Remember to use "Nodatatypes"
       argument or "NoDataTypes=YES" tooltype to go back to the (much
       faster) IFF loading routines.

14/01/00

   o Zeus - The Write ARexx command now takes the argument 'NoExpand'
       which stops it expanding Control Codes.  Please add this argument
       to any Write where data may be displayed which is not from the
       scriptset or a CC in some way!  Example: in the WedLock
       CheckWaitMail.zeus,
            DoWrite:
               Write OutLine 'UseMoreYNC' 'NoExpand' DOpts
               IF RC = 2 THEN DOpts = 'NOMORE'
               IF RC < 1 THEN fin = 1
            Return
   o MsgControl - At least some of the Yes/No/Continuous prompts don't
       take any notice of the YesChar, NoChar or ContChar Language
       settings! It appears you can only respond with Y, N or C. The
       ARexx/Zeus provided GetYesNo seems to work correctly. I'll fix
       this, but be warned that some ARexx scripts (e.g simple file list)
       merely check for Y/N/C etc. without consulting the Language data.
   o Zeus - Fixed problem with YNC prompts not responding with lower case
       YesChar, NoChar or ContChar language settings.

16/01/00

   o ZMailer - New item added to the logfile, "Unlisted system",
       indicating that the calling/called node could not be found in the
       nodelists.

17/01/00

   o ZMailer - New debug log item, "Transfering <x> as <x>" indicating
       the name an outbound bundle/packet is sent as.
   o ZMailer - Some modem strings were hardwired into the code when they
       are available from prefs.
   o ZMailer - On a BUSY signal when dialing out, ZMailer will clear the
       window and write BUSY in the System field (the title bar text
       disappears far too quickly).
   o ZMailer - Far better handling of EMSI password failures.  ZMailer
       now states that the password has failed in a 'fake' connection
       (showing the BBS name as "Bad password") and offers no transfer
       protocols.  Previously, the connection would just be dropped on
       incoming calls.  Also the more detailed log line: "No valid
       passwords for secured AKAs and no valid unsecured link possible"
   o ZMailer - On XPR transfers (e.g. ZedZap), ZMailer double checks the
       number of errors and timeouts and aborts if any reach 10.

19/01/00

   o ZMailer - Now shows full texts in the GUI if you widen the window -
       previously the text was clipped to the smallest size.

20/01/00

   o FileControl - Long time bug found!  When doing new file scans with
       the SimpleList commands, you might have noticed that sometimes,
       when reaching the end of the screen, the header of an area was
       shown but no files were (even when you know there are new files in
       that area). This was a FileControl bug and is now fixed.

08/02/00

   o ZMailer & Prefs - Uses an extensible prefs system now.  The old
       prefs file is maintained for compatibility, but now each ZMailer
       line gets its own config file in Zeus:Config/Msg/Mailer<X>.iff.

09/02/00

   o ZMailer - Extended some buffers which could overrun easily in some
       circumstances.
   o ZMailer & Prefs - New config item in `Externals': Data Handler.
       When some data is received from the modem, such as Caller ID
       information, the command specified here will be called with the
       line number and data as arguments, like this:
       <command> <line number> <data> <data...>
       e.g.
       Test.rexx 4 CID = 192.168.1.7
   o Control - Was overwriting your colour preferences with those from
       the IFF background when deiconified, when using the built in IFF
       routines.
   o ZMailer - Fixed case when a few pixels in the top border were
       cleared to grey.
   o ZMailer - When getting a nodelist error calling out (unknown node,
       undialable), ZMailer will set the title bar of the window to the
       error message as well as sending it as a RESULT message.
   o ZMailer - New ARexx command, LASTCONNECTSTR, which returns the last
       modem connection string in RESULT when RC=0 or when RC=5 no
       connection since ZMailer was loaded.
   o ZMailer - New ARexx command, LASTCALLER, which returns the name of
       the last user/sysop to connect in RESULT when RC=0 or when RC=5
       nothing has called since ZMailer was loaded.

