13/09/00

   o FileControl - ARexx SetFileArea was limiting multipath string
       lengths to 64 chars, not 108, and could have caused memory
       overruns.  
   o FileControl - ARexx SetFileArea wasn't reading PathList option,
       taking it as Path instead..
   o FileControl - ARexx SetFileArea wasn't saving MultiPaths. <sigh>
   o FileControl - ARexx SetFileArea wasn't adding MultiPaths if none
       already existed for that area. <sighsighsigh>

22/09/00

   o File Headers - struct GeneralFileCfg now includes ULONG MinFree,
       which will soon be acted upon by FileControl and FileConfig to
       allow SysOps to specify how much space to leave on any file path.
       (e.g. you need space on Files: to generate your file lists, set
       some KB in FileConfig->General and Zeus will always leave that
       free, by going onto another MultiPath or reporting out of space
       to an uploader.)
   o FileConfig - Added Min Free (KB) to General window.
   o FileControl/zmf.library - Added support for Min Free to the upload
       path finding routines.
   o zmp.library - Upload path finding routines recognise partitions of
       2TB (with 512b block sizes).  This will filter into everything else
       eventually.

01/10/00

   o ZMP - Found that with a 4KB stack, ZMP runs low on %RESCAN and runs
       out on %FORCERESCAN (boom..).  ZMP now enforces a minimum stack
       size of 16KB.

07/10/00

