27/12/00

   o ZMailer - Found cause of TelSer crashing on start up: it doesn't
       like being opened and closed repeatedly. Now, ZMailer doesn't
       send your hang up string when opening the device for the first
       time (normally this contains a ^ - which does a device close/open).
       Also, never use multiple ^ in a modem command string, more than
       one is redundant anyway.
   o zeus.library - "Prefs/System->Settings->Last calls in list" now
       trims calls by age in days. This previously was the actual
       number of last call entries to keep, which is not good enough if
       you want day-by-day statistics.
   o Zeus - The Shared->ExtraSaved data structure now holds file, message
       and user statistics for the current day and dated records.
       Implementation of this data is gradually being rolled out to the
       rest of Zeus.
   o Zeus - New ARexx function PAGESYSOP. This currently only handles the
       paging statistics (how many pages today, when the record number was
       made, etc). Perhaps will become a hook for an external pager.

28/12/00

   o MsgControl, FileControl, ZMailer - Implemented statistics recording.
   o Devkit: To access the new statistics, look into
       (SharedData *)GetShared()->Extra->es_#? -- the ExtraShared
       structure.
   o Zeus - New Control Codes from Zeus:

       CC 350:    Files up today.
       CC 351:    Files down today.
       CC 352:    Bytes up today.
       CC 353:    Bytes down today.
       CC 354:    Record no. of files up in a day.
       CC 355:    Date and time of record files up in a day.
       CC 356:    Record no. of files down in a day.
       CC 357:    Date and time of record files down in a day.
       CC 358:    Record no. of bytes up in a day.
       CC 359:    Date and time of record bytes up in a day.
       CC 360:    Record no. of bytes down in a day.
       CC 361:    Date and time of record bytes down in a day.
       CC 362:    Messages written online today.
       CC 363:    Record messages written in one day.
       CC 364:    Date and time of record messages in a day.
       CC 365:    SysOp pages today.
       CC 366:    Record pages in one day.
       CC 367:    Date and time of record pages in a day.
       CC 368:    New users today.
       CC 369:    Record new users in one day.
       CC 370:    Date and time of record new users in a day.
       CC 371:    Record calls in one day. For number of calls today,
                  see CC 100.
       CC 372:    Date and time of record new users in a day.
   o Zeus - The Line structure contains statistics data about the current
       user's call:
   UWORD                 le_Uploads;         /* Number of files uploaded IN THIS CALL - copied to last callers list */
   UWORD                 le_Downloads;       /* Number of files downloaded */
   ULONG                 le_UploadsBytes;    /* Number of bytes uploaded */
   ULONG                 le_DownloadsBytes;  /* Number of bytes downloaded */
   UWORD                 le_Messages;        /* Number of messages written IN THIS CALL */
   UWORD                 le_StatsFlags;      /* Flags for statistics only */
       This data is copied into an extended LastCallers structure when the
       call ends. Due to this, the existing Zeus:Config/LastCallers.dat is
       incompatible! Software which access the last callers list in the
       legal way through zeus.library functions (GetShared(), lock
       semaphore, access, release) will still work fine. Either the 1.4
       update will delete or convert the existing .dat file...

01/01/01

   o ZAmiMirror.rexx - Supports MiamiFTP or ncFTP. Did you know MiamiFTP
       copies the directory part of a get command for the local file name?

02/01/01

   o ZGate - EEEEEEK! If you wrote a newsgroup message and a mailing list
       message, and the mailing list message was exported by ZMP after the
       newgroup one, the mailing list message would be "addressed" in it's
       headers as if it was going to the newsgroup!
   o ZMP - Sorts the ZMP Stats file if it detects that it's out of correct
       order. Ordering is done on the area number - so if you want ZMPStat
       in alphabetical order, sort your actual areas config on the BBS.
       MsgConfig *will* do this eventually.

04/01/01

   o RecentCallers - Added this ZDoor, which is a perfect clone of the RRR
       recent callers door for /X (which was written specifically for
       Digital Candy BBS in the UK). (NB: I do not have nor have seen the
       RRR source code nor do I currently own a copy of the /X door).
       You need to give it your BBS name as there's only 16 characters
       space for it, so for neatness you can specify a short name rather
       than have the program mess up a longer name got from Prefs/System.

       Usage:
       LINE/N/A,BBSNAME/A,RN=REALNAMES/S,SS=SHOWSYSOP/S,SL=SHOWLOCAL/S
         LINE           - Line number
         BBSNAME        - A short, 16 characters or less, name for your BBS
         REALNAMES      - Use real names instead of user's aliases
         SHOWSYSOP      - Show calls made by the SysOp (as defined by the name in
                          Prefs/System)
         SHOWLOCAL      - Show calls made by on local lines

       Remember that quotes around the BBS name need to be escaped:

            ZDoor '"RecentCallers 'line' \"DIGITAL CANDY\""'

   o AmiEx - Fixed this AmiExpress door emulator. Inputs now work. (Does
       that make it look like it was a trivial fix? Perhaps it was, but
       finding it wasn't ...)

