08/01/02

   o mbzeus - Those of you with a keen eye will have noticed that running
       'mbmanager maint' on mbzeus areas never really did very much.
       This is because the code for maintenance merely copied the data
       in the given message base from one file into another. So, I've
       re-written it. Call Maintenance on a message area using the mbZeus
       msglib will result in all the deleted messages being removed, and
       the base being renumbered from 1 to <max msg number> (although this
       introduces issues with users no longer having their correct himsg
       pointers, but I don't care - just run msgmaint like me and have any
       users find where they were up to manually).
       Seems to work too. Here's my netmail/email before and after:
       ZeusText.900.BACKUP            42283940 ----rwed Today     20:24:21
       ZeusText.900                   39179150 ----rwed Today     20:43:49
       ZeusHdr.900.BACKUP              1473612 ----rwed Today     20:25:07
       ZeusHdr.900                     1361888 ----rwed Today     20:43:49
       A new message was exported correctly so HighSentByNet still works.

11/06/02

   o zmf.library - New MSGID random number generator when creating fido
       headers - as used in ZMP. Should no longer cause fake dupes when
       (e.g.) running PostMan several times in one second.

26/06/02

   o ZGate - Added a hack to avoid processing "References" lines if they
       appear in email, as with all the cases I've seen them in email
       they have no relation to the thread of the message and it throws
       ZGate's database out of whack.

27/07/02

   o ZNewsXfer - The KillFile never actually worked. This is why I could
       never get rid of Tim Rue or SG's messages. Now, however, I've
       looked at the source and it was obviously broken. It's now fixed.
       The killfile only kills on the Message-ID: line -- so find some
       repeating, unique part to kill on - usually the idiot's email
       address is part of the Msg ID.
       The string comparision is done on a unix wildcard basis -- so only
       the wildcards * (any number of characters) and ? (one character)
       are valid. You may like to use this example as the basis for your
       killfile:

         *threeseas@earthlink.net>
         *sg@erols.com>

28/07/02

   o ZNewsXfer - When running with more than one socket, any socket which
       went unused (e.g. no groups with more than 3 new messages in would
       mean that the 4th socket wouldn't need to be utilised) was at risk
       of server side timeouts. ZNewsXfer now sends fake No-Operations
       (NNTP has no no-op command) -- simply a newline is sent.
   o MsgMaint - Command arguments template had unnecessary /K attributes.

29/07/02

   o Netmail Mapper - Fixed mungwall hit.
   o zeus.library / zmf.library - Replaced 1993's "quick hack" sorting
       routines (which were, I think, O(N^2)) with an O(N log N) merge-
       sort. The speed increase is considerable across Zeus.
   o UserEditor - I was a bit puzzled as to why the UserEditor was still
       very slow, even with the new sort algorithm. So, I removed the 3rd
       party progress bar - woosh, UED sorts & redraws the user list
       instantly. In fact, it would be instant even with the old sorting
       algorithm. The progress bar is now permanently removed.

30/07/02

   o ZMP - In the unlikely event of the ZMPstat data file,
       MsgNetStats.dat, being corrupted, ZMP will attempt to handle this
       and clean the file, retaining data if possible.

31/07/02

   o ZMP - Now has the ability to have netmail areas defined for AKA
       addresses instead of a zmp.cfg NODE address.
   o SigEditor - Fixed crash on SIG delete. It might not have taken so
       long if there were any code comments at all that I could have
       read. But everything is undocumented.
   o SigEditor - Made some very quick hacks at the SigEditor.
       Many bugs squashed. It never freed its memory, but does
       (at least, I hope) free all of it now. Also a crash on exit should
       now be fixed.

07/08/02

   o ZGate - The bug where ZGate would dump large amounts of memory in to
       the <mail dir>/ZGate.dat file came back today. However, I was able
       to snapshot my machine and make the error reproducable. I *hope* I
       have finally found and fixed the problem now.

13/08/02

   o ZMailer - Fixed buffer overrun in the recent log window.

20/04/03

   o ZMailer - Fixed buffer overrun in the recent log window :)
   o ZGate - Implemented mailing list server, using ZGate.CFG line
       "HOSTEDLIST". Works in much the same way as a subscribed list
       but also mails messages from an echo to every listed subscriber.
       Docs to come, also a way for people to add/remove themselves to/
       from lists much like AreaFix (mostly like a small Rexx script to
       call from ZMP).

22/04/03

   o ZGate - Still crashes on very long headers, I can't fix it yet so I
       put the line buffer up to 32KB per line as a work around.

23/04/03

   o ZPOP3Xfer - Major update: added config file, multiple servers, rules
       for mail filtering (substring search and DOS wildcards). Just needs
       debugging and speeding up (the pattern matching code is fairly
       slow).
   o ZPOP3Xfer - Debugged.. looks reliable enough to use, so out goes
       Poppy and in comes ZPOP3Xfer for a trial period.

20/05/03

   o ZNewsXfer - Added GMT offset support, if correctly set in Internet
       preferences.

29/06/03

   o MsgControl - Limit searches for */_^ highlight characters in
       messages to 120 characters. Should speed up display of large
       messages. Also reworked logic to improve word highlighting,
       particularly incorrect interpretations of / in URLs.

******************* Zeus 1.5 Fixed Feature Set **********************

08/10/05

   o ZNewsXfer - Added support for NNTP servers in different timezones.
       New argument "TIMEZONE/K/N" on command line. Example, for
       www.readfreenews.net servers in Miniapolis and me in the UK,
       use "... timezone -6".
   o ZMailer - Fixed problem with telser device where it would cause
       ZMailer to hang if the connection dropped before we were sent
       the CONNECT (or immediately afterwards).

16/09/06

   o ZSMTPxfer - now works, only issue seems to have been that it hung on
       reading the header. Now fixed.

******************* Zeus 1.6 Fixed Feature Set **********************

02/09/07

   o mbzeus - reverse message scanning has never worked, now fixed.
   o zmf documentation - ScanMsgHdrs was never documented, now fixed.
   o zmf.library/MsgControl - private UserMsgData structure has been
       extended.
   o MsgControl - three new ARexx commands, [Init|End|]MsgScan. An
       interface onto the fast message header scanner in the Zeus
       message library API. Previously this was available only to
       binary software. Can be significantly faster than the old
       ARexx method of using LoadMsg with no body text for individual
       message numbers due to the buffering mechanism. Updated
       example script messages/scanmsgs.zeus to use this.

08/02/09

   o Completed work started on Installer script in 2007.

******************* Zeus 1.7 Fixed Feature Set **********************

